{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "865210c0c39c4a78b56ee514a4cc4d25",
    "m_Title": "Equilateral Triangle Simplexes",
    "m_Content": "In order to turn a square based grid into a equilateral triangle grid, I need constants to convert to a triangular lattice. I followed the reference below to do this.\n\nSkew Value 0:\nWill define the triangular lattice points. This needs to be done by turning the triangle grid back to a square grid.\n\nSkew Value 1: \nWill determin the shape of the rhombus. This value needs to be a constant so the rhombus shape is the same shape as two equilateral triangles side by side. This results a conversion value from squares to triangles.\n\nSkew Value 2:\nThis is the height from centroid to vertex in an equilateral triangle with unit sides, or the distance from center to a vertex when drawing the triangle centered.\n\nReference: https://catlikecoding.com/unity/tutorials/pseudorandom-noise/simplex-noise/",
